  "packageSize": 316573,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Cynicszm/FlatFiles",
  "published": "2026-09-29T15:53:24.82Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "9.1.2 - SpanParsingHooks.Unchanged is now int.MinValue rather than -1, so that no length a hook asks for can be mistaken for it; anyone who compiled against 9.1.0 or 9.1.1 has to rebuild, because a const is copied into the calling assembly. The three ways of asking a column to parse a value - the string overload, the span overload and the typed parse a mapped property uses - now share one implementation of what a value means, and the record and format paths are compared with each other as well, by tests that drive the same input down every path and insist they agree. One custom mapping no longer takes every column beside it through the array of values: asking for a record number cost a thirteen column mapping 1.69 MB per ten thousand records and now costs 0.62 MB. No breaking changes to any signature.",
